<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Albert II, Duke of Saxony</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1250–1298</span> · <a href="/centuries/13th-century">13th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Albert II was an Ascanian <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/duke-of-saxony">Duke of Saxony</a> who ruled jointly with his brother John I and then John's sons until the partition of 1296, which gave him the lands around <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wittenberg">Wittenberg</a> on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/elbe">Elbe</a>, the Duchy of Saxe-Wittenberg, while his nephews received Saxe-Lauenburg. A supporter of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rudolf-i-of-germany">Rudolf of Habsburg</a>, he married Rudolf's daughter Agnes. His line later won the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/saxons">Saxon</a> electoral dignity, confirmed by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/golden-bull-of-1356">Golden Bull of 1356</a>.</p></div>
